  "findings": [
    "Windows file/SQLite/PostgreSQL queue acceptance fills JobQueue and ControlCommandQueue to the configured 4096 pending-record cap, rejects overflow, and acknowledges the queued records.",
    "ControlCommandQueue tests reject commands exceeding 16 KiB; SQLite and PostgreSQL queue runs record the owner-matched worker batch and acknowledgement counts.",
    "The PostgreSQL capacity evidence records p50/p95 enqueue latency and process RSS for this Windows 11 host; values are environment-specific measurements.",
    "File, SQLite, and PostgreSQL Paper worker evidence covers six dispatch-to-ack crash/restart boundaries with idempotent recovery.",
    "Hosted Ubuntu CI run #590 independently matches the Podman-reviewed queue semantics for file, SQLite, and PostgreSQL: all three reach 4,096 pending entries, acknowledge all 4,096, reject overflow (and ControlCommandQueue oversize input), and recover all six worker crash boundaries. CI records are bound to R21-AC01; performance figures remain host-specific."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Capacity/latency/RSS numbers describe the recorded Windows host and run configuration; they are not portable performance guarantees.",
    "Crash recovery uses Paper fixtures and does not demonstrate live venue recovery."
  ]
